[{:db/id "q-52538/selection/099fdf0281820709ce1d4e437ba833ccfea116b5a3cba3506f943a01c7d9ab5d" :answer/id #uuid "f2acc9f0-5722-5eb2-82d3-0dd8c1896a33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52538/selection/a108e5b2e24d64a2d35607b439010b8418af87f0c169610d879cfee4243c7e43" :answer/id #uuid "c45560aa-2300-5383-8b3d-0af649a859d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+5)^{2}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52538/selection/e28c318f8d37a6e8a9660fb6e67357db557219d8df695164c235c397efec0ff3" :answer/id #uuid "727a8079-9680-5f98-8042-d4a670d2b9cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5(x-2)^{2}+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52538/selection/63efd587a87918b534b9d4fcc29185e7d1895eb4aaa4972f536b9c63db3c387e" :answer/id #uuid "d390abc9-01bc-51af-8632-2e8080576716" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5(x-2)^{2}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52538/selection/d1da37ddf949e1c25239a91438ba5a14d9c50112c8820e3769ec90a4cf1a1b46" :answer/id #uuid "95981072-0715-57c0-a38e-ba6003674a8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5(x-2)^{2}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-52538/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "77af4ed2-3504-598c-91f6-efd54383dad1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-52538/selection/e28c318f8d37a6e8a9660fb6e67357db557219d8df695164c235c397efec0ff3" :answer-field/choices ["q-52538/selection/099fdf0281820709ce1d4e437ba833ccfea116b5a3cba3506f943a01c7d9ab5d" "q-52538/selection/a108e5b2e24d64a2d35607b439010b8418af87f0c169610d879cfee4243c7e43" "q-52538/selection/e28c318f8d37a6e8a9660fb6e67357db557219d8df695164c235c397efec0ff3" "q-52538/selection/63efd587a87918b534b9d4fcc29185e7d1895eb4aaa4972f536b9c63db3c387e" "q-52538/selection/d1da37ddf949e1c25239a91438ba5a14d9c50112c8820e3769ec90a4cf1a1b46"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-52538" :question/id #uuid "71c7c147-b250-5795-95ad-bdcd7961182a" :question/math-academy-id "q-52538" :question/problem "Rewrite $5{x}^{2}-20x+25$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $5.$ So, we take out a factor of $5$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n5({x}^{2}-4x+5)\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-4x+5\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+5\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${2}^{2},$ writing the constant term $5$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2}}_{⏟}-{2}^{2}+5\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-2)^{2}-{2}^{2}+5\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(x-2)^{2}+1\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5({x}^{2}-4x+5) & =5((x-2)^{2}+1) \\\\  & =5{(x-2)}^{2}+5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =5{(x-2)}^{2}+5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-52538/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "564f2cf7-aaaf-5dea-b619-a560c3151fcc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-52538"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-52544"] :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-140332/selection/02ec04510a55856304da2e54c8229db3f249ee1d9e6dcaea78c17f40f9736c13" :answer/id #uuid "c1a90a10-21d5-55c5-b19b-db7c91f5ebb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{4}-{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140332/selection/ba2060c5ba70c7d82bd1a89df85dcf9be8b9bc08c45c76b097fcffb6941fccb2" :answer/id #uuid "be426baa-55bb-560d-b0aa-d9fae1f28a32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}-{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140332/selection/8f2f4dd9f9221cd845ece206788ad23fecfaa0186be3324e1f88c8c3ff52cfd1" :answer/id #uuid "63d69f5a-b2cb-549c-9b83-29dfc975d696" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}-{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140332/selection/1a7f88b3ee924d25208e8fdbf8fe0ae640639717240ed8d8cdcbc173b9ff940f" :answer/id #uuid "89e6201a-ffd8-5a86-9c93-6e41bfded996" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}-{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140332/selection/ef86d261d43b4a93e7d451175be1610f9a5bd8473a55ee5d8407b7c8631f85e7" :answer/id #uuid "b37ccd3f-3d21-50eb-b0b7-7222d68bdbf8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6-{(x-2)}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140332/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4cea6423-0808-507a-b960-5b857f67e506" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140332/selection/1a7f88b3ee924d25208e8fdbf8fe0ae640639717240ed8d8cdcbc173b9ff940f" :answer-field/choices ["q-140332/selection/02ec04510a55856304da2e54c8229db3f249ee1d9e6dcaea78c17f40f9736c13" "q-140332/selection/ba2060c5ba70c7d82bd1a89df85dcf9be8b9bc08c45c76b097fcffb6941fccb2" "q-140332/selection/8f2f4dd9f9221cd845ece206788ad23fecfaa0186be3324e1f88c8c3ff52cfd1" "q-140332/selection/1a7f88b3ee924d25208e8fdbf8fe0ae640639717240ed8d8cdcbc173b9ff940f" "q-140332/selection/ef86d261d43b4a93e7d451175be1610f9a5bd8473a55ee5d8407b7c8631f85e7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140332" :question/id #uuid "dbe926ee-762a-5e17-9033-da4b3ab1c650" :question/math-academy-id "q-140332" :question/problem "Rewrite $-({x}^{2}-x-2)$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "We begin by completing the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-x-2\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}x-2\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2},$ writing the constant term $2$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}x+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-2\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-2\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-({x}^{2}-x-2) & =-({(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\  & =-{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}-{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140332/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a85fece-e40f-543c-b3c3-ae43a5175808"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140332"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140333/selection/3229bf53ee9b9f6573f4a2ab85ea31a2cc75c9643c454e4b93949023a39ffc75" :answer/id #uuid "170d0483-4547-501d-add3-92ddac362220" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}-{(y+\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140333/selection/91a149303559720644aadb1eb8238dc6f31e1543f3f0eaa49b169430b01e7f5a" :answer/id #uuid "d30291c7-e575-59e8-85d7-cee0a0dac214" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}-{(y+\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140333/selection/ab02491a00e631aebf8624fe0ac5653cb9af03c9d07bd056e2c06fa1181eeeea" :answer/id #uuid "ab58645a-9bcf-567b-a560-cffe5e08eb98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}-{(y+\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140333/selection/1036039539e712d992086e3e28981734547a8b6216c8a0d581daf478358f8f1b" :answer/id #uuid "550266fd-139d-51f4-a898-c1630f39f3ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{161}{4}-{(y-\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140333/selection/0e9ecacd5246d173bb20cbf07445ec9634d0eb891c67153a6698c438911b170f" :answer/id #uuid "edf98753-a420-52e4-b4b8-24bc1fc005aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "61-{(y+18)}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140333/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "83bbfda0-2a2c-5dd5-8b70-0051a76a29af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140333/selection/ab02491a00e631aebf8624fe0ac5653cb9af03c9d07bd056e2c06fa1181eeeea" :answer-field/choices ["q-140333/selection/3229bf53ee9b9f6573f4a2ab85ea31a2cc75c9643c454e4b93949023a39ffc75" "q-140333/selection/91a149303559720644aadb1eb8238dc6f31e1543f3f0eaa49b169430b01e7f5a" "q-140333/selection/ab02491a00e631aebf8624fe0ac5653cb9af03c9d07bd056e2c06fa1181eeeea" "q-140333/selection/1036039539e712d992086e3e28981734547a8b6216c8a0d581daf478358f8f1b" "q-140333/selection/0e9ecacd5246d173bb20cbf07445ec9634d0eb891c67153a6698c438911b170f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140333" :question/id #uuid "46c23e9e-2448-5acd-a673-896062dd7b10" :question/math-academy-id "q-140333" :question/problem "Rewrite $-({y}^{2}+9y+20)$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "We begin by completing the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}+9y+20\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}y+20\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2},$ writing the constant term $20$ last:\n\n$$\n{{y}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}y+{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}+20\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(y+\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}+20\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(y+\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-({y}^{2}+9y+20) & =-({(y+\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =-{(y+\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}-{(y+\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140333/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a85fece-e40f-543c-b3c3-ae43a5175808"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140333"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140375/selection/cb7c77bb3abaa62bac56b85db825f1ab8abe2dacdb058dcabaf1172d4b4a1e7e" :answer/id #uuid "c3b9008d-9206-597d-a1c5-2ef2ab34c51e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{(x+\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140375/selection/68179c6ee840c82aa018f9e8cf493efd229d212d54014803cc35ae139f60c344" :answer/id #uuid "10f0d321-45e5-571e-9088-9b32d863c82e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{(x+\\frac{5}{3})}^{2}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140375/selection/63a052a58573c273231511c034be77e50873c0f4474c211dc8c21564e3567f40" :answer/id #uuid "33f035f9-63da-5f06-961e-a84b459b7687" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{(x+\\frac{5}{3})}^{2}-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140375/selection/53b51f18ac6f2fea0f5add3e8a32ec1def45a3009ecfcba4eb0c5ba670964f3f" :answer/id #uuid "eec27287-96a4-590a-8bdb-a239184f3279" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{(x+\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140375/selection/b3e22f36572b54c29e03c82131d644ace88d3a9bb853fe61b30e3f9e2d466589" :answer/id #uuid "ecc17d5a-6198-58e3-89f4-6b0518ec8740" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{(x+\\frac{10}{3})}^{2}-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140375/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1bfc736e-c31a-5fdc-bc6f-23b0ba457c0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140375/selection/53b51f18ac6f2fea0f5add3e8a32ec1def45a3009ecfcba4eb0c5ba670964f3f" :answer-field/choices ["q-140375/selection/cb7c77bb3abaa62bac56b85db825f1ab8abe2dacdb058dcabaf1172d4b4a1e7e" "q-140375/selection/68179c6ee840c82aa018f9e8cf493efd229d212d54014803cc35ae139f60c344" "q-140375/selection/63a052a58573c273231511c034be77e50873c0f4474c211dc8c21564e3567f40" "q-140375/selection/53b51f18ac6f2fea0f5add3e8a32ec1def45a3009ecfcba4eb0c5ba670964f3f" "q-140375/selection/b3e22f36572b54c29e03c82131d644ace88d3a9bb853fe61b30e3f9e2d466589"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140375" :question/id #uuid "71b04e78-c149-5982-a00d-24fd0a042784" :question/math-academy-id "q-140375" :question/problem "Rewrite $6{x}^{2}+10x-\\frac{11}{6}$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $6.$ So, we take out a factor of $6$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n6({x}^{2}+\\frac{5}{3}x-\\frac{11}{36})\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+\\frac{5}{3}x-\\frac{11}{36}\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{5}{6}\\cdot x-\\frac{11}{36}\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{5}{6})}^{2},$ writing the constant term $\\frac{11}{36}$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{5}{6}\\cdot x+{(\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}-\\frac{11}{36}\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}-{(\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}-\\frac{11}{36}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression::\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6({x}^{2}+\\frac{5}{3}x-\\frac{11}{36}) & =6({(x+\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}-1) \\\\  & =6{(x+\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}-6\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =6{(x+\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}-6\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-140375/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "564f2cf7-aaaf-5dea-b619-a560c3151fcc"] 